The '''eleventh series''' of ''[[The Great British Bake Off]]'' began on 22 September 2020. It was presented by returning host [[Noel Fielding]] and new host [[Matt Lucas]], who replaced [[Sandi Toksvig]],<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/matt-lucas-great-british-bake-off-noel-fielding-sandi-toksvig-new-series-channel-4-a9393391.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/matt-lucas-great-british-bake-off-noel-fielding-sandi-toksvig-new-series-channel-4-a9393391.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |title=Great British Bake Off: Matt Lucas to replace Sandi Toksvig as host of Channel 4 show|first=Adam |last=White |work=The Independent |date=11 March 2020 }}</ref> and was judged by returning judges [[Paul Hollywood]] and [[Prue Leith]]. The first three episodes were extended to 90 minutes instead of the usual 75 minutes. The bakers were announced on 15 September 2020.<ref name="bbc bakers">{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-54151631 |title=Great British Bake Off: 2020 contestants revealed|date=15 September 2020 |work=BBC }}</ref>

Filming of the eleventh series was delayed by the [[COVID-19 pandemic in the United Kingdom|COVID-19 pandemic]]; originally scheduled to take place in April 2020, it was pushed back to July 2020.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://deadline.com/2020/07/the-great-british-bake-off-back-in-production-1202991744/ |title='The Great British Bake Off' Is Cooking Again After A Covid Delay & Will Premiere Later This Year |first= Jake |last=Kante|work=Deadline |date=22 July 2020}}</ref> Filming the series normally takes place over 12 or 13 weeks on the weekends, but due to the pandemic, the cast and crew had to live in a "self-contained biosphere" ([[Down Hall]] Hotel near [[Bishop's Stortford]] with a skeleton staff),<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.essexlive.news/news/essex-news/great-british-bake-off-full-4515914 |title= Great British Bake Off: Full contestant line up revealed for 2020 show filmed in Essex|first=Alice |last=Cunningham|date= 15 September 2020|work=Essex Live}}</ref> and filming took place in a marquee tent in the garden of the hotel over a period of six weeks.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/news/tv/2020-09-14/great-british-bake-off-covid-scare/ |title=The Great British Bake Off filming was almost shut down after COVID scare |work=Radio Times |first=Patrick|last=Cremona|date= 14 September 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/news/tv/2020-09-14/bake-off-2020/ |title=When is The Great British Bake Off on TV in 2020? |first=Kimberley |last=Bond|date= 14 September 2020|work=Radio Times }}</ref>  The contestants and crew had to undergo a period of self-isolation after filming had ended.

The series was won by [[Peter Sawkins]], with Dave Friday and Laura Adlington finishing as the runners-up. Sawkins is the first [[Scottish people|Scottish]] winner of the programme, and also the youngest winner in the show's 10-year history, at the age of 20.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/live/2020/nov/24/the-great-british-bake-off-2020-final-live|title= The Great British Bake Off 2020: final – as it happened|date=24 November 2020|work=Guardian|accessdate=25 November 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-55056352|title= The Great British Bake Off crowns its 2020 winner|date=24 November 2020|work=BBC News|accessdate=25 November 2020}}</ref>

Series 11 was released on [[Netflix]] in the [[United States of America|U.S.]] as Collection 8. It premiered on 25 September 2020, with each episode available three days after the UK air date.

