==Specials==

Two compilation episodes of ''The Great British Bake Off: Best Bits'', showing highlights from the previous ten series, were shown in the weeks after the final.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv-programme/e/mvx7cx/the-great-british-bake-off-best-bits---e1-the-great-british-bake-off-best-bits/ |title= The Great British Bake Off: Best Bits |first=Alison |last=Graham |work= Radio Times }}</ref>  These were followed by two further specials focusing on the previous 10 winners: ''The Great British Bake Off: The Winners''.<ref>{{cite web |url= https://www.hulldailymail.co.uk/news/celebs-tv/great-british-bake-off-winners-4799104 |title=Great British Bake Off winner Nancy Birtwhistle rubs shoulders with the elites on new show|work=Hull Daily Mail |date=15 December 2020 }}</ref> The first episode covered the first five champions, the second the last five.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.channel4.com/programmes/the-great-british-bake-off-the-winners/on-demand/ |title= The Great British Bake Off: The Winners |work=Channel 4}}</ref>

Two specials were commissioned for the festive season:

=== ''The Great Christmas Bake Off'' ===

The Great Christmas Bake Off features James Hillery from [[The Great British Bake Off (series 8)|Series 8]], Ruby Bhogal from [[The Great British Bake Off (series 9)|Series 9]], Jamie Finn and Rosie Brandreth-Poynter both from [[The Great British Bake Off (series 10)|Series 10]]. An Extra Slice presenter Tom Allen, took over Noel Fielding as co-host with Matt Lucas, as Fielding welcomed the birth of his second child prior to filming and was on paternity leave.

For the signature challenge, the bakers were given 3 hours to create 12 miniature [[panettone]]s. Prue's technical challenge required the bakers to make a quick [[Christmas pudding]] (with [[mincemeat]] made from scratch), to be cooked in a microwave and served with a [[crème anglaise]], in 1 hour and 15 minutes. The showstopper challenge asked the bakers to make an illusion cake to depict their ultimate Christmas day feast in 4 hours.
